By the way, there are two solar eclipses in '94.  The first is an
annular eclipse (the moon is directly in front of the sun, but
due to their relative orbital positions, the moon isn't quite big
enough to completely cover the sun).  It is on 10 May.  It begins
in the Pacific, crosses the middle of Baja, and crosses the US
from the Southwest, through the Midwest and Northeast.  It ends
in Morocco.

The second is a total eclipse on 3 November.  It starts in the
Pacific, crosses the lower third of South America and the South
Atlantic.  It passes just south of the African continent and ends
south-east of Africa.


